WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Pleasure to be here.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm happy to talk to you
about this book.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.005 size:88% position:44%
This is basically about
how the Trump Presidency

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Donald Trump himself
had no interest in maintaining

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.143 size:88% position:44%
a functioning government
through the transition

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the previous
administration,

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.346 size:78% position:39%
and you've said that,
"Only Donald Trump

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.182
could make a book about
bureaucracy interesting."

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can you just explain that
real quick?

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.819 line:92%
-He's electrified the material

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.087 line:92%
So, the way he did it is great

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
That he did it by starting out
firing the 500 people

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were supposed to handl
his transition

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.795 line:92%
the day after the election

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:29.763 line:92%
So, they're supposed to go i

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
and learn how the government
works,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there are people waiting
to explain to them, like,

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
how the nuclear arsenal
is managed

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
or how we stop the ebola virus
from becoming a pandemic,

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.508 line:92%
and they just did not show

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, when I realized
I had a book

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that this material
was very good --

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.846
when I realized I was the firs
person to talk to the person

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:47.981 line:92%
who handled the nuclear weapons,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, like, nobody had bothere
to get the stuff.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to this day,
you can wander around,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they've never
taken the time

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have the thing
explained to them,

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he has no interest
whatsoever in it.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.295
And then the question is,
like, what does that mean?

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what does it mean
if the President,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.933
who's supposed to be running
this 2 million person operation,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:10.703
actually does not care, or wants
to dismantle parts of it?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.140
And I think was it means is,
like, there are all these risk

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.675 line:92%
that the government manages.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, some
are really obvious,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
like you don't want nuclea
bombs going off

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:19.813 line:92%
when they shouldn't go off

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you don't want
viruses spreading,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you don't want, like,
the research that's happenin

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.154
so we can grow food in a
different climate not to happen.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, there's all this stuff,
and so that was --

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.826 size:81% position:41%
that was the beginning
of the thing for me.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was, like, these risks
are all more probable

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's not there.
-And you know,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:42.202 size:84% position:42%
obviously, he spends
a lot of time attacking

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.603 line:92%
sort of what government mean

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the people who choose
government as a life,

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.174 line:92%
and a lot of these people are --

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, these are
civil servants.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.444 size:81% position:41% line:92%
These are bureaucrats.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We saw them in the impeachmen
hearings, right?

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.014
The minute you see them, you
realize, like, the deep stat

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just people who know what
they're talking about.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Right, that's it.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is it.
There's no deep state.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I promise you. I was there.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's not there.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's no secret elevato
that goes down?

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.426 line:92%
-It's a very shallow state

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:09.028 size:88% position:44%
-You added to this book,
in the paperback version

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wrote about Art Allen --
is that the name?

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, that's right.
So, you see --

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, when the government
shut down

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.002 line:92%
in the beginning of the year

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.906
800,000 people were sent hom
and told they were inessential

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.040 line:92%
So, I asked for a list --

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who are these inessential
government workers?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't a whole list, but it
was a whole big list.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.480
I didn't know -- I said, "I want
to find one of these guys.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took the name at the top
Arthur A. Allen.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is how it works
as a reporter.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.219 line:92%
You just take the first name

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's kind of how I roll.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But I call him up.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, "You're inessential.
What did you do?"

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.261 line:92%
He's the only oceanographe

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Coast Guard
Search and Rescue Department

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.865 line:92%
He got there in the late '70s.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.334
He -- you know, he kind of
stumbled into the government

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.204
He finds after a few years
that everybody is asking him

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
questions that if he doesn't
know the answer to,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, nobody knows
the answer to,

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're kind of scienc
questions, like,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.978
"How long can someone surviv
in the water in a survival sui

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
before they die
of hypothermia?"

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
He starts answering these
sorts of questions,

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.117 line:92%
and he goes out and he sees --

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.853
he wakes up and goes and watches
a search and rescue,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:11.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he sees a storm come acros
the Chesapeake Bay,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a boat get lost
with this little girl

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and a mom on it.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.430
And when I was sitting in hi
living room talking to him

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
about it, he said, "You want t
know why I do what I do?"

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he pulls a clipping ou
from his --

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.270
like, a yellow newspaper
clipping out from his bookshelf,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.906
and it's about this mom
and her daughter who died

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the Coast Guard
couldn't find them.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.443 size:75% position:38%
And he realizes that
what we don't know,

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:33.513 size:84% position:42%
that we need to know,
is how that boat drifts

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
after it's capsized
that these people were on.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.151 line:92%
And he spends his career,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is what
he's been doing --

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is, like,
an inessential worker

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the minds
of the Trump Administration --

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
is he spends his career
tossing stuff out

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.561 line:92%
into the Long Island Sound

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.531
and studying how it drifts
depending on what it is.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.233 size:88% position:44% line:92%
An upside down sailboat,

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
a fat person, a...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
A person on a life raft,
or whatever it is.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what you need to understan
is that at any given time

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's an unbelievable
amount of crap

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
floating on the ocean,
and a surprising amount of i

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are Americans.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.250 line:92%
Like, Americans have a --

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a gift
for getting lost at sea.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.853
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-No, no, no, I'm deadly serious,

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.256 line:92%
like 13 people a day on average.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.024 line:92%
Ten get rescued, three die

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.292 line:92%
And a lot of times they di

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they don't know
how they drifted.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.131 line:92%
He makes a science of it.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when he teaches
the Coast Guard

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.271 size:88% position:44%
how you follow an object
that's drifting at sea,

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:33.673
they start finding people wh
never would have been found.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:37.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
Days after he releases thi
information to the Coast Guard

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
a 300-pound man runs out of hi
window of a cruise ship

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:47.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
into the ocean, and three hour
later, they find he's gone

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.055 size:78% position:39% line:92%
They know where he --

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
They end up finding out
when he went off the ship.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
That man is dead any other
time in human history,

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.929 line:92%
and because of this guy's work

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
they plucked him
out of the ocean.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is a guy who,
thousands of people are aliv

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of his work,
and nobody knows who he is

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he has no impulse to
market it

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.241 line:92%
or tell anybody about it.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what's
in the government.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.078 line:92%
And that's what we're telling --

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're telling these peopl
they're inessential?

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's crazy.
-And do you think

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:18.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we have a Presiden
who obviously,

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.019 line:92%
you know, is a braggadocio

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
and these people
have great humility,

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:24.490
do you think he values them less
because they're not --

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because they don't know
how to sell themselves.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's just --

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're almost
the opposite of him.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know how to do things
-Yeah.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Right?

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-And they --

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they know things.
-Yeah.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're like the key
to the future,

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they don't know how
to persuade you

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:47.480 size:84% position:42% line:92%
